## The conformance suite itself

The OpenID Foundation conformance suite is **not** vendored here. It is used as the prebuilt
container images `registry.gitlab.com/openid/conformance-suite` and
`registry.gitlab.com/openid/conformance-suite/nginx`, which are independent works:

> MIT License, Copyright (c) 2019-2020 OpenID Foundation
> <https://gitlab.com/openid/conformance-suite>

OpenID, OpenID4VCI, OpenID4VP and the certification marks are trademarks of the OpenID
Foundation. This harness is not affiliated with or endorsed by the OpenID Foundation, and a
green local run is not an OpenID certification.

`scripts/bootstrap-official-scripts.sh` downloads `run-test-plan.py` and its helpers from
that same repository into `runner/vendor/` (not committed) so the official driver can be run
for comparison. Those files stay under the MIT license above.

## Runtime and build dependencies

Resolved from package repositories at build/run time; not vendored.

| Dependency | Where | License |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `httpx`, `urllib3` | Python runner (`runner/requirements.txt`) | BSD-3-Clause / MIT |
| TestNG | Java bridge | Apache-2.0 |
| Jackson (`jackson-databind`, `jackson-core`, `jackson-annotations`) | Java bridge | Apache-2.0 |
| ExtentReports (and its transitive freemarker, gson, rxjava) | Java bridge | Apache-2.0 |
| JCommander, SLF4J API | TestNG transitive | Apache-2.0 / MIT |
| `mongo`, `postgres`, `nginx` images | the compose stack | SSPL-1.0 / PostgreSQL / BSD-2-Clause |

The plans, variants, condition adjudication and expected-failure schema follow the
OpenID Foundation's own `run-test-plan.py` behaviour so that results are comparable with the
official driver; that logic was reimplemented here against the documented REST API and the
suite's log format, and is covered by this repository's license.
